  "source_transcript": "My crush said she'd never date a boy shorter than her, so I strapped stills under my pants. Overnight I went from the shortest boy in school to the tallest. I told everyone it was a growth spurt. I hit my head on every door. Girls I'd never talked to suddenly needed things from the top shelf. And one day, so did she. And for the first time, my crush had to look up at me. The basketball coach signed me without watching me play. Every week, my pants got shorter, and I blamed the stills. Then came the championship game. It was the last second, and the whole school was screaming. I jumped for the dunk, and both stills snapped in midair. I crashed onto the court, two broken sticks poking out of my pants. The ball rolled in. The gym went silent. My crush walked onto the court, and I stood up, ready to be shorter than her again. I wasn't. I was still an inch taller. The growth spurt had been real for months. She stood on her toes, still looking up and kissed my cheek. Okay, you win.",
